8e893bf-9ffa-4baf-831a-6c950947902e","position":{"commit_sha":"8bff09f8b1967a75f6e56b193a38e859e175a875","position":"1787484672946174001-a8e893bf-9ffa-4baf-831a-6c950947902e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e9b12454de85966995116646cece73dd9d90378dd288855f4a895c26a28fd5c2","event_uuid":"063f7b4f-ff32-45e7-aeab-bc757907b93b","position":{"commit_sha":"c02ff81c9c38ef3bdc6caae9676904d757b7b215","position":"1787484905029779001-063f7b4f-ff32-45e7-aeab-bc757907b93b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for deterministic P10/P6 findings: added a `## Testing` section that mirrors all existing ticket-level verify commands and split compound acceptance criteria into independently observable outcomes. No implementation target, public-description scope, typed default/coercion contract, or runtime behavior changed.","timestamp":1787420577450123001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for blocking E6/F1 finding: added a row-by-row manual editorial proof that compares each Description cell with its Key, Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells and requires the completed review to be recorded on the ticket. Also clarified that F19 authorizes the follow-on Description column, documented the single-source rationale for field metadata, and split the remaining compound criteria. No automated content heuristic or runtime change was added.","timestamp":1787421279853084001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third plan-review remediation for blocking E6/F1 finding: marked the four editorial criteria `[non-codebase]` and bound their manual proof to a ticket comment containing reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and the completed row-by-row result. Also made the missing/empty-metadata failure-injection test explicit and clarified that `public_description` is the authoritative external prose while existing comments remain internal notes. Scope remains configuration-documentation generation only; runtime behavior is unchanged.","timestamp":1787421890547400001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution preflight counted 100 emitted fields in the 697-line schema module. Adding required field metadata in place would put formatting headroom at risk under the absolute 800-line limit. Recorded  as the exact section-boundary extraction named by the approved plan and expanded the module-size proof to cover both schema modules. This material correction intentionally invalidates the prior F19B attestation and its parent material pin.","timestamp":1787423913935762001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction. The exact extraction path is src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py. The preceding comment lost that path when its shell quoting interpreted Markdown backticks. The five-path file-impact event and four verification commands contain the correct value.","timestamp":1787423938051679001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation preparation is complete. The dedicated worktree /Users/joeoakhart/docs-f19b-config-correction is based on dbf351c3fea200c665e777bc3ba081ed3ebbc2b0 and includes the landed F19A correction. The refreshed plan review passed with a signed attestation and no findings. I claimed the ticket before any file edit or validation gate. Implementation will attach field-local public descriptions, extract VerifyConfig along the approved section boundary, update the generator, regenerate the reference, and run the recorded verification commands.","timestamp":1787480004746123001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation and local validation completed.\n\nEditorial attestation\n\nReviewer: RebarBotNava using joeoakhart@navapbc.com\nReviewed at: 2026-08-23T10:33:30Z\nRows reviewed: 100\n\nEvery generated Description cell was compared with its Key, Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells. Each description states a user-visible effect or operational consequence. No description merely restates its type, default, or lifecycle. The review found no unresolved row.\n\nValidation evidence\n\n- The focused description contracts failed in five expected cases before implementation and passed in five cases after implementation.\n- D1 passed. The generated configuration reference is current.\n- D2 passed with 73 focused tests.\n- D3 passed with no new or increased complexity. `_config_schema.py` has 790 lines and `_config_schema_verify.py` has 242 lines. Both are below the 800-line limit.\n- D4 passed. Lint completed every repository check, and mypy reported no issues across 641 source files.\n- An AST comparison against dbf351c3fea200c665e777bc3ba081ed3ebbc2b0 confirmed unchanged annotations, defaults, and default factories for all 100 typed fields.\n- F19A commit 7e2e6afb27026969b86c922285390ba75aa5124b is included in the worktree base. The refreshed plan attestation remains certified at dbf351c3fea200c665e777bc3ba081ed3ebbc2b0.\n\nThe implementation changes the five recorded paths only. It adds no prose validator or character restriction.","timestamp":1787481253506892001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final local commit preparation completed.\n\nA parallel F10 change advanced `origin/main` to 7e3d9d0b12f4e01dbe258926c76fe2be1a941efc after the first F19B validation. The F19B commit rebased onto that main commit without conflict. The rebased commit is 39d5951897744fc96712d2bf69f19189857a59da with Change-Id I50c345b797caf91a2527281240dd5b4450b19be2.\n\nAll four recorded verification commands passed again after the rebase. The focused suites passed with 73 tests. Lint passed, and mypy reported no issues across 641 source files. The commit ticket trailer resolves. The worktree is clean, the plan attestation remains certified, and the ticket remains claimed in progress. No Gerrit push has occurred.","timestamp":1787481568370081001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI run 32634565434 completed with failure after 1,861 seconds. Classification is test-failure. Three held-out checks could not find the string-read fields require_plan_review_for_close, require_plan_review_for_claim, and require_completion_verification_for_close in src/rebar/_config_schema.py. The local reproduction matched with three failures and one pass. No retry or corrective change occurred before classification. Root cause evidence shows that the patch extracted VerifyConfig while the configuration-read gate treats _config_schema.py as the canonical schema source. The corrective hypothesis is to restore VerifyConfig to that source, move only low-level validation helpers into the existing _config_coercion.py module, and remove historical comments that duplicate ticket or ADR context. This preserves the field markers and module-size limit.","timestamp":1787484098372222001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction evidence\\n\\nThe held-out reproduction now passes all four marker cases. The wider configuration suite passed 401 tests. The complete lint target passed Ruff, formatting, complexity, configuration ownership, configuration reads, environment registry drift, comment hygiene, and raw Git write checks. Type checking passed 640 source files. Configuration reference drift checks passed. The module-size contract passed with src/rebar/_config_schema.py at 793 lines. origin/main remains at 7e3d9d0b12f4e01dbe258926c76fe2be1a941efc, which is the patchset parent.\\n\\nCI_RESULT\\n{\"run_id\":\"32634565434\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"duration\":1861,\"failure_type\":\"test-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"Three held-out configuration-read cases could not find string-read VerifyConfig fields in src/rebar/_config_schema.py.\",\"fixes_applied\":[],\"retry_count\":0}","timestamp":1787484672946174001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2157 now has patchset 2 at commit ce496143fe1f72a07efeb0173da37013262ec446. The patchset parent is origin/main at 7e3d9d0b12f4e01dbe258926c76fe2be1a941efc. The Change-Id, DCO sign-off, and canonical rebar-ticket trailer are preserved. Gerrit removed the stale LLM-Review and Verified votes when the patchset was uploaded.","timestamp":1787484905029779001}],"created_at":1787417361912923001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6bfb79a4-f64e-4f04-bccb-9d7862478efd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ec70-3cb3-9a94-4645"},{"link_uuid":"3ead61d2-637b-44ec-8707-6d2b1fb65a4d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"79ef-23b3-04f2-42d2"}],"description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration reference enumerates key, type, default, and lifecycle data from typed dataclass fields but provides no public setting descriptions. It cannot serve as the external settings contract until each emitted key explains its user-visible effect. F19 explicitly authorizes this Description-column enrichment as corrective follow-on scope beyond the closed generator baseline; generated ownership remains unchanged.\n\n## Plan\n- Add concise `public_description` metadata to every dataclass field emitted through `_SECTION_CLASSES`, co-located with each field so generator introspection remains the single source of truth and a sidecar description registry cannot drift.\n- Treat `public_description` as the authoritative external setting prose; existing code comments remain internal implementation notes rather than a second generated contract.\n- Preserve field types, defaults, factories, coercion, and runtime behavior.\n- Extend `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` to require nonempty description metadata and render a Description column.\n- Fail generation when an emitted field lacks a description.\n- Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md`.\n- Add focused tests for complete metadata, table escaping, generated drift, and an injected missing or empty description that fails with the offending key named.\n- Review every generated Description cell against its key plus adjacent Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells; require a user-visible effect or operational consequence rather than a restatement, then record the reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and completed row-by-row result in a ticket comment.\n- Keep `src/rebar` modules below the absolute 800-line limit. Use an existing configuration-section seam if an extraction is required.\n\n## Testing\n- `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py -q`\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt)`\n- `make lint && make typecheck`\n- Manual non-codebase proof: inspect every generated Description row against its Key, Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells; record reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and the completed row-by-row result in a ticket comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every generated typed key has one nonempty public description.\n- [ ] The injected missing or empty metadata test fails with the offending key named.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Each description identifies a user-visible effect or operational consequence, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row type, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row default, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row lifecycle, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] Generated Markdown escapes table-sensitive content correctly.\n- [ ] Typed field annotations remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Default values remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Default factories remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Configuration coercion remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Configuration runtime behavior remains unchanged.\n- [ ] `_config_schema.py` remains within the absolute module-size limit.\n- [ ] Focused generator tests pass.\n- [ ] Focused typed-configuration tests pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Type checking passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Attach public descriptions to typed configuration fields and import the extracted VerifyConfig section."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py","reason":"Hold the extracted VerifyConfig dataclass and its field description metadata within the module-size policy."},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Require and render public descriptions."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate configuration rows with descriptions."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Pin description completeness, escaping, and drift behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","66c6-2fe5-4850-4297"],["relates_to","79ef-23b3-04f2-42d2"],["relates_to","ec70-3cb3-9a94-4645"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"66c6-2fe5-4850-4297","parent_status_uuid":"484360c1-a6e9-400e-aabb-20abf987df4f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["documentation","f19b","configuration"],"ticket_id":"5df8-2209-2c49-42c8","ticket_type":"task","title":"F19B generate descriptions for every typed configuration key","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Generated configuration reference is current"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py -q","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Description and typed configuration contracts pass"},{"command":"python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt) && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt)","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Complexity and module-size contracts pass for both schema modules"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"D4","dd_text":"Source lint and type checks pass"}]},"source_event_uuids":["a6238a01-3471-4dea-a23b-1a5f0090bf03","95bcdeed-b0dd-4840-8acb-03b5f0b7f292","484360c1-a6e9-400e-aabb-20abf987df4f","42a4336f-6eb6-4c86-9ca4-373512619fa7","26b2bc43-1a10-4522-bb79-6239d73cffe1","0ce1da08-e138-49ef-a6d5-28b89e690844","0e716d44-2e0a-4402-8008-ffc22a148196","6bfb79a4-f64e-4f04-bccb-9d7862478efd","2a5fd3dc-7213-4187-aa49-8c5865e3c921","3ead61d2-637b-44ec-8707-6d2b1fb65a4d","a8e893bf-9ffa-4baf-831a-6c950947902e","063f7b4f-ff32-45e7-aeab-bc757907b93b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787484905029779002,"uuid":"d9a2d75e-1a4f-4863-adce-ca0889a2e2e3"}